-- title:
--   Regularity of the blow-up chart at places integral for j
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a positive natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ subject to the guard conditions `hℓ12` ($\ell \equiv 11 \bmod 12$) and `hℓM'` ($\ell \mid M'$). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and assume `hι`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` is the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which by `hK` is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield of $L((t))$ generated over $L$ by the image under coefficientwise extension [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian local discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with `hj`: as a Laurent series, $j$ is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-invariant. Let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy `hϖt`: $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$ (the finite chart of the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec} A[j]^{\mathrm{int}}$ and $\operatorname{Spec} A[j^{-1}]^{\mathrm{int}}$). Let $y \subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the Drinfeld chart witness, a seven-clause conclusion summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ pulled back from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma \varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, such that: (i) $e$ carries the image of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (i.e. on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, $\tau$ induces, after reading coefficients through any $\iota$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the substitution by the scaling matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`), $\tau$ preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for such $\gamma, \tau$ congruent to the identity modulo $y'$ there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ intertwining $\tau$ through $e$ and the germ map, fixing the constants, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $\theta(X_k) \equiv \sum_i M_{ik}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ik} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ik}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes of $S$ above $\sigma\varpi$, neither containing both $X_0, X_1$, whose leading linear forms $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ have $a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ prime to $q$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ above $\sigma\varpi$ with leading form $X_0$, the germ of $a \in C$ lies in the contraction of $P$ precisely when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0 \in A$, and the difference is carried by $e$ to the class of some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \geq 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b) \in W^2$ with one entry a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   There are then given a specific such point $z$ with $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of its stalk (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ (`hy'`) with supersingular ideal (`hss'`) satisfying `hy'y`: $y'$ corresponds to $y$; and a specific presentation at $z$, namely a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1 \equiv$ `drinfeldForm q W₁` modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` states that this data satisfies the same seven clauses (i)–(vii) just listed, for $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ and this $z, y'$.
--
--   Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ which by `hJ` is the infimum of the set of ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the contraction along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ (\text{completion}) \circ (\text{germ at } z)$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which by `hB` is the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra; informally $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ with $B \subseteq W$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses are: `hR1`, that $C \leq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h$ a unit of $W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant in the sense that each level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $W$ is matched through $\rho$ with the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of a pair $(\overline{\gamma}, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image under some $\tau$ (for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$) of the centre $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$; that an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   The conclusion is a single assertion: for every $f \in K$ with $f \in B$, and every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ (an [`AlgebraicCurve.Place L ↥K`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22), that is a valuation subring of $K$ other than $K$ itself, containing the image of $L$ and a principal ideal ring) such that $\operatorname{ord}_P(j) \geq 0$, one has $\operatorname{ord}_P(f) \geq 0$; here $\operatorname{ord}_P$ is minus the logarithm of the $\mathbb{Z}^{m_0}$-valued adic valuation attached to $P$. Thus every element of the blown-up chart $B$ is regular at each place at which $j$ is regular.
--
--   This is the regularity (integrality) statement for the $\varpi_t$-blow-up $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the finite chart of the two-chart integral model: on the non-cuspidal part of the modular curve, where $j$ has non-negative order, every function in $B$ is again of non-negative order. It is used in the construction of the end chart of the integral model at the supersingular points, in the auxiliary level-one frame with the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ diamond guard, by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_endChart_finiteType_isLocalization_pole_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd).
